  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nThunderstorms will likely increase later in the day on Saturday and \ninto Saturday night. There will be the potential for damaging winds \nduring this time. Also cannot rule out an isolated tornado, although \ndamaging winds and heavy rain will be the primary threats. There is a\nhigh potential for the need for an additional flood watch primarily \nnear and north of I-70. Will hold off until tonight with uncertainty \non axis of heaviest rainfall. Going into Sunday there is the \npotential for additional heavy rain, damaging winds, and the \npotential for an isolated tornado. Added severe wording into the HWO \nfor Sunday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nWhile temperatures will warm for this weekend there is a lot of\nuncertainty in just how warm it will be as temperatures will be \nhighly dependent on thunderstorms and associated cloud cover. Made \nsome adjustments down with temperatures in spots. Still getting some \nlocations across the tri-state area reaching around 100 heat index \nfor Saturday and most of the area for Sunday. Will continue to \nmention heat potential for the weekend, but not confident enough to \nissue any headlines.",
